infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Two lenses on a hot Node process
  desc Snapshots answer what is retained; flame graphs answer where CPU goes
  compares
    - label Heap snapshot
      children
        - label Memory question — what is retained, by whom
          desc The reachable object graph at one instant
        - label Sort survivors by retained size
          desc Shallow size hides the tiny container anchoring a huge subtree
        - label Three-snapshot diff names the leak
          desc Objects allocated during work, still alive two snapshots later
        - label Retaining path points at the anchor
          desc A global Map, a closure, an un-removed listener, a timer
        - label Leak signature — monotonic growth
          desc RSS rises and never returns to baseline
    - label CPU flame graph
      children
        - label CPU question — where the time goes
          desc Call stacks sampled thousands of times a second
        - label Frame width = share of CPU
          desc Not call count, not call order; widest frames are the cost
        - label Bare top means high self time
          desc The frame does the work — a tight loop, sync JSON.parse, a regex
        - label Plateaus are the optimization targets
          desc Wide flat tops, not a tall hot caller
        - label Capture with --cpu-prof or --prof
          desc Open the .cpuprofile in DevTools; 0x renders the flame SVG
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b
